🏥 Level 1 – Hospital Core SQL Training (25 Questions)
Objective

This module covers 70–80% of real-world hospital data analyst responsibilities.

Focus areas:

Time-based aggregation

KPI calculation

Ratio metrics

DISTINCT counts

Basic JOINs

Financial summaries

Operational reporting

Clinical activity analysis

These 25 exercises simulate real hospital analytics tasks.

🔹 Module 1 – Volume & Utilization (Operational KPIs)

Total encounters per year.

Monthly total encounter volume (2015–2020 trend).

Monthly inpatient encounter count.

Monthly inpatient ratio (inpatient encounters / total encounters).

Encounter distribution by encounter_class.

Monthly encounter volume by organization.

Monthly encounter volume by provider.

Annual visit frequency distribution per patient (identify heavy users).

🔹 Module 2 – Patient Metrics

Annual distinct patient count.

Monthly distinct patient count.

Average annual visits per patient.

Patient gender distribution.

Patient age distribution by age group (e.g., 0–17, 18–34, 35–49, 50–64, 65+).

🔹 Module 3 – Inpatient Analytics

Average Length of Stay (LOS) for inpatient encounters.

Monthly average LOS trend.

Average age of inpatient patients.

Average LOS by organization.

🔹 Module 4 – Financial KPIs

Monthly total revenue (SUM of total_claim_cost).

Monthly average revenue per encounter.

Annual revenue by organization.

Average encounter cost by encounter_class.

🔹 Module 5 – Clinical Activity Analysis

Top 10 most frequent diagnoses (conditions).

Monthly count of new diagnoses.

Top 10 most frequent procedures.

Top 10 most prescribed medications.

Skills Covered in Level 1

GROUP BY and aggregation

Date and time handling (date_trunc, extract)

COUNT(DISTINCT)

KPI numerator/denominator logic

Basic joins

Financial aggregation

Operational reporting logic

Clinical frequency analysis

Outcome After Level 1

After completing these 25 exercises, you should be able to:

Build hospital operational reports

Calculate inpatient metrics

Produce financial summaries

Analyze provider workload

Support executive dashboard reporting

Write production-grade SQL for healthcare analytics
